{"name":"Amelia","hex":"#beccc2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Amelia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Ericaceae – synonym of Pyrola (wintergreens).","A taxonomic genus within the family Tortricidae – synonym of Aphelia (certain tortrix moths)."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from the Germanic languages.","The alternative name for Amelia Courthouse, Amelia County, Virginia, US."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Amelia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amelia (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Amelia is a 2009 biographical film about the aviation pioneer Amelia Earhart. The film stars Hilary Swank as Earhart, and co-stars Richard Gere, Ewan McGregor, Christopher Eccleston and Joe Anderson. The film was directed by Mira Nair and based on The Sound of Wings by Mary S. Lovell. The film received negative reviews, with critics polarized over the performances and criticizing the film's story. It was also a box-office bomb, grossing $19.6 million against a budget of $40 million."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Ameliaposter09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amelia_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6a/Ameliaposter09.jpg/250px-Ameliaposter09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Ameliaposter09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6a/Ameliaposter09.jpg/250px-Ameliaposter09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmeliaposter09.jpg"}],"sounds":{"Amelia":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/LL-Q